 containing both characters' spoken voices; it serves as the voice-timbre reference for <Subject 1> (S1) and <Subject 2> (S2), preserving the exact spoken Chinese dialogue and the natural conversational pacing of the original recording.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + audio reference] The target video is built as four shots, one per spoken line. <Subject 1> (S1) opens with line one around the start; <Subject 2> (S2) delivers line two; <Subject 1> (S1) returns with line three; <Subject 2> (S2) closes with line four. Both characters lip-sync to the original Chinese dialogue using <Audio 1> as the voice-timbre reference, and the four cuts land on the turn-taking of the audio.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3], [Shot 4]): fully_preserved - the orange tabby cat's striped fur, amber eyes, dark-red scarf, metal bracer, bipedal stance, and scruffy charm are retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3], [Shot 4]): fully_preserved - the orange-and-white dog scholar's pointed ears, round wire-rimmed reading glasses with chain, beige shirt, brown satchel, bamboo-slip waist pouch, and studious posture are retained.\n<Audio 1>: reference - the target speakers follow <Audio 1>'s voice timbres, natural pacing, and exact Chinese dialogue content without copying the original signal as the final audio track; the four shot changes fall on the four spoken lines.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is rendered in a cinematic, painterly wuxia-fantasy style with soft moonlight key lighting, warm lantern fill, and a slightly desaturated color palette of jade green, pale gold, and ink black. The clip follows the about 17-second dialogue in <Audio 1>, cut into four shots that each carry one spoken line.\n\n[Shot 1] A wide establishing shot frames a moonlit ancient-style garden. Mossy stone paving runs across the foreground; a shallow ornamental pond dotted with pale lotus leaves sits in the middle distance, framed by slender weeping willows whose long fronds trail into the still water. An arched wooden moon-gate glows faintly at the far end, and a cluster of blooming osmanthus bushes scatters pale-yellow petals through the calm air. A low stone lantern on the left casts a warm amber pool of light. The night sky above is clear and dusted with dimly twinkling stars. <Subject 1>, the bipedal orange tabby cat with the dark-red scarf and metal bracer, sits on a flat garden stone to the left of the lantern, chin tilted upward toward the sky. <Subject 2>, the orange-and-white corgi scholar in the round wire-rimmed reading glasses, beige shirt, and brown satchel, stands to the right beside the lantern, an open leather-bound book cradled in both paws and a bamboo brush tucked behind one ear. <Subject 1> (S1) slowly lowers its gaze from the sky, turns toward <Subject 2>, and speaks in a soft, mildly wistful young voice referencing <Audio 1>'s timbre, <d>[Chinese] 今天的星星，好像比昨天暗了一点点。</d>\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.8, the shot cuts to a medium over-the-shoulder shot from behind <Subject 1>'s left shoulder, looking across at <Subject 2>. Weeping-willow fronds softly frame the foreground; the lotus pond glimmers in the background bokeh. <Subject 2> (S2) does not look up from the open book. One paw rests on the page as if checking a data point; the other paw taps a small abacus-like tally pinned to the satchel strap. <Subject 2> (S2) delivers the long line in a measured, slightly pedantic male voice referencing <Audio 1>'s timbre, <d>[Chinese] 根据我的观测记录，心之星的亮度在过去七天里下降了百分之十二点七三。不过嘛，也可能是大气折射——</d> after a brief natural pause inside the line the head tilts a little more casual on the trailing clause, gaze drifting back to the page.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:11.6, the shot cuts to a close-up of <Subject 1>. The lantern's warm rim light catches the cat's amber eyes; osmanthus petals drift slowly past the lens. <Subject 1>'s ears flatten a fraction, the whiskers pull back, and the gaze drops deliberately downward toward the book in <Subject 2>'s paws. <Subject 1> (S1) interrupts in the same soft voice now sharpened with dry suspicion, referencing <Audio 1>'s timbre, <d>[Chinese] 你骗谁呢。你书都拿反了。</d> A small, knowing smirk lifts one corner of the cat's mouth on the final syllable.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:14.0, the shot cuts to a close-up of <Subject 2>. The camera reveals, in soft focus, that the book's spine is facing upward and the inked characters are indeed upside-down relative to <Subject 2>'s eyes. <Subject 2>'s ears twitch; the reading glasses slide a fraction down the snout on their thin chain. <Subject 2> (S2) looks up, meets <Subject 1>'s gaze, then glances back down at the book. In a flustered, slightly higher-pitched voice that still references <Audio 1>'s timbre, <Subject 2> (S2) stammers with a small stumble between the repeated word, <d>[Chinese] 这是、这是逆向阅读法。</d> The glasses glint off the lantern light as <Subject 2> defensively turns the page anyway, paws slightly trembling. Hold on <Subject 2>'s embarrassed half-smile as a single osmanthus petal settles onto the upside-down page, then let the frame fade to black on the audio's tail.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA quiet nocturnal garden ambience continues throughout: a soft breeze moving through willow fronds, faint rustle of osmanthus petals falling into still water, the occasional low chirp of a night cricket, and the gentle ambient hum of the stone lantern's warm pool of light. No traffic, no modern sounds.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "值"}], "flags": {}, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "Input Text (Prompt)", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#533", "size": [436.140380859375, 366.0526123046875], "pos": [-1527.300537109375, 6121.9619140625], "id": 138, "properties": {"ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {"value": true}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 11}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#222", "widgets_values": ["| 占位符                               | 含义 / 用法                            |\n| --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `(S1) (S2)`                       | 稳定说话者 ID，跨镜头不变；复合如 `(S1,S2)` 表示一起说 |\n| `<d>[Language] ...</d>`           | 对白/歌词，**逐字保留原文语言**，只放语言标签+原文，不翻译   |\n| `<scenetrans>`                    | 同一句对白跨过一次镜头切换时，连接处用，并说明音频跨越继续      |\n| `<cutoff>`                        | 语音被视频结尾截断时使用                       |\n| `says in an off-screen voiceover` | 画外音专用短语；其后补一句「画面内角色嘴唇保持闭合」         |"], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "title": "说话对话占位符", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#000", "size": [453.94744873046875, 331.8420104980469], "pos": [-1998.617431640625, 4835.89794921875], "id": 165, "properties": {"ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 12}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#222", "widgets_values": ["顺序固定，缺一不可：\n\n1. `subject_definitions` — 定义每条被参考内容及其标签\n2. `summary` — `[任务类型]` 前缀 + 目标视频与参考关系概述（如 `[reference generation + audio reference]`）\n3. `retention_analysis` — 每条参考如何被保留/转移（用 `fully_preserved` / `partially_preserved` / `attribute_transfer` / `weak_reference`，音频用 `fully_copy` / `partially_copy` / `reference` / `weak_reference`）\n4. `detailed_description` — 按播放顺序逐镜头描述（正文英文，对白用 `<d>`，参考标签在首次出现处插入）\n5. `overall_soundscape`\n6. `non_diegetic_music`\n"], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "title": "说话对话占位符", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#000", "size": [453.94744873046875, 331.8420104980469], "pos": [-1992.1180419921875, 5197.34716796875], "id": 166, "properties": {"ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 13}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#222", "widgets_values": ["| 标签            | 含义                                | 典型写法      